action, quote: when a mom goes into a bakery and says make me a happy birthday cake for my child,\n  - id: 27ac3400-5b48-44cf-8512-d7ed449511a2, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Sotomayor Demands the Difference, quote: I just don\'t want to be affiliated with that concept of rainbowness at a wedding, any kind of wedding.\n  - id: e4adb4cf-240c-465e-a007-d32e5d601205, idea_id: 16-111, title: Gorsuch Presses Yarger on the Consequence of Disagreement, quote: What if we disagree with you? Then what follows?\n  - id: 375deeb0-cd96-4f9f-9d9a-28d09b2e934e, idea_id: 16-111, title: Sotomayor\'s Seven Commissioners Test, quote: stop fighting the belief; accept the hypothetical -\n  - id: 899dca58-eae5-4d2e-a6dc-eb881fedc454, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Kagan\'s Makeup Artist Empathy Test, quote: makeup artist, I think, might feel exactly as your client does, that they\'re doing something that\'s of -- of great aesthetic importance to the\n  - id: eb449c8a-2c6a-4b09-978b-360718422aee, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Kagan\'s Anniversary Chef Test, quote: How about that? So, Your Honor, if I\n  - id: d305c0d3-6656-4c80-9ede-0dfe00a5d898, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Kagan\'s Master Chef Speech Test, quote: Well, Your Honor, you have to confront that issue in every First Amendment case, if you\'re -\n  - id: 9c87c85d-4b15-48da-bc78-5325bc868f70, idea_id: 16-111, title: General Francisco\'s Imperfect Cake Test, quote: And here you have a cake that is essentially synonymous with a traditional sculpture except for the medium used.\n  - id: 5308096b-d5a1-4b25-8763-cb538450629d, idea_id: 16-111, title: Roberts\' Cake Hypothetical and Rights Question, quote: Could he have said I\'m not going to make a cake for, you know, celebrating events that aren\'t permitted in Colorado?\n  - id: 55422e79-2b0e-4d66-bfca-a679802f1dd2, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Kennedy\'s Wedding Cake Attendance Test, quote: Does the baker have to attend that wedding and -- and help cut the cake?\n  - id: 5c4748d1-6afb-4daf-be1c-e3a72d5b7374, idea_id: 16-111, title: None, quote: None\n  - id: 6740e154-d6b5-44b0-b525-0dbba53bcbf3, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Sotomayor\'s Community Membership Test, quote: we can\'t compel you to like these people,\n  - id: 333b2d0c-18f1-476d-94c0-7eb6f61d5c50, idea_id: 16-111, title: None, quote: None\n  - id: 531ba2b2-1307-4ccd-98c4-691ee89ee62b, idea_id: 16-111, title: Roberts Demands Equal Treatment for Gay Couples, quote: problem in connection with their marriage, again, whatever it is, contract dispute, something like that, they would have to provide representative services to someone\n  - id: d21e2ca9-7ca3-43de-9c1b-9d4ded9623d7, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Alito\'s Office Door Contrast, quote: Well, we want a civil union. Well, we won\'t accommodate that either.\n  - id: 7855d9d8-6395-46ee-a1ef-944cbe0c931c, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Alito\'s Forced Words Paradox, quote: someone can be compelled to write particular words with which that person strongly disagrees.\n  - id: 27d38b08-1813-4fbf-bc6a-0c62600dbff3, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Sotomayor\'s Fork Test, quote: The primary purpose of a food of any kind is to be eaten.\n  - id: 0a097f0e-cad5-4beb-bff0-ceca3b795f00, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Scalia\'s Three Business Examples, quote: \n  - id: 2a89d03b-7c38-44b9-9665-c0d5d929d17a, idea_id: 16-111, title: Compliance Versus Personal Expression Debate, quote: In Mr. Phillips\'s case, they said it wasn\'t his message. It\'s simply compliance with the law.\n  - id: 3f5493b1-45dc-41bb-9586-2a96c1d78429, idea_id: 16-111, title: Justice Alito\'s Commercial Transaction Test, quote: as was the case with the parade in Hurley,\n  - id: bdd02ff2-7501-4490-83f0-8b8afc6aacb8, idea_id: 16-111, title: None, quote: None\n  - id: 994ec296-fc2b-4d63-a8c1-337dcc8b10e5, idea_id: 16-111, title: None, quote: None\n  - id: e4fdc8c7-7488-45e8-be51-8ba75c5f49e2, idea_id: 16-111, title: Roberts Separates Commerce from Expression, quote: And, therefore -- or gay. And, therefore, he wouldn\'t sell them a wedding cake which he would sell, gladly, to anybody outside -\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
